<!--Post: 26--><!--Time: 1085170559-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST26"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pharaoh<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pharaoh<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 1:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Anyone know more details about the purported ciphers in the new BTK letters?  I&#39;d love to know what the status is &#40;solved?, unsolved?, how many?&#41;.  I&#39;ve read that they think BTK might be a fan of word-puzzle magazines, b/c his ciphers were similar to something recently published in one.  Any idea what magazine or puzzle they&#39;re referring to? <BR> <BR>Tom, you&#39;re probably familiar with obtaining stuff like this from the work you&#39;ve done on the Zodiac page - is there any hope of seeing these ciphers anytime soon or are they on lockdown since the case is still open?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 26-->
<!--Post: 28--><!--Time: 1085177980-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST28"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ibedamom<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ibedamom<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 3:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->also, could factor x refer to the old comic series?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 28-->
<!--Post: 29--><!--Time: 1085178096-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST29"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 3:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pharaoh, when I get copies &#40;notice I said <i>when</i>&#41; I will post them. Until then, I&#39;m pretty much in the dark.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 29-->
<!--Post: 128--><!--Time: 1085840507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST128"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 29, 2004 - 7:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom ,I found some information on what was in the letters at ezboard Crime &amp; Justice. The date is 4/14/04 the poster is The GoldenBoy37. The btk wrote the new letter some what like the Z did in his paradice slaves note,only upside down and backwards in the shape of a L. It reads wrong address, and diekaf &#40;fake ID&#41;. The word ruse was also in the puzzle.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 128-->
<!--Post: 133--><!--Time: 1085854810-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST133"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 29, 2004 - 11:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am rather suspicious of intelligence data collected by someone called &#34;GoldenBoy37.&#34; Maybe it&#39;s accurate, maybe not. <BR> <BR>BTK certainly seems to be into word puzzles. Maybe one day we will see one.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 133-->
<!--Post: 137--><!--Time: 1085931740-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST137"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 30, 2004 - 8:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found more than one list from the 5/5/04 note and they all have this as what was in the first page of the last note from btk.----1.A SERIAL KILLER_______   2.DAWN 3.FETISH  4.FANTASY WORLD  5.THE SEARCH BEGINS  6.BTK HAUNTS  7.PS&#39;s  8.MO-ID RUSE  9.KITS  10. TREASURED MEMORIES  11.FINAL CURTAIN CALL  12.DUSK  13.WILL THERE MORE  &#40;he left out the &#34;BE&#34; &#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 137-->
<!--Post: 138--><!--Time: 1085934704-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST138"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 30, 2004 - 9:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, Here is another part of the btk letter.I read that this was found at crime librery.com . It looks like the btk would like a book written about him, and these should be the chapters. 1.ALL AMERICAN CITY  2.A CHILLING DISCOVERY  3.BIND THEM,TORTURE THEM,KILL THEM  4.DIFFERENT WORLDS COLLIDE  5.VANISHING ACT  6.GHOST BUSTERS  7. THE NEXT STEP  8.COLD CASE SQUAD  9.PROFILE  10.AFTERMATH  11.BTK RETURNS  12.BIBLIOGRAPHY  13.THE AUTHOR <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 138-->
<!--Post: 148--><!--Time: 1086031107-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST148"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 31, 2004 - 12:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sandy, I believe that these are the chapters as set out by the editors of Crime Library, not BTK himself in a letter.  These predated the most recent letter&#40;s&#41;.  In your 8:42 am letter,  above, those are the chapters that BTK put in the most recent letter, if the letter is genuine.  He patterned them after the Crime Library chapters. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 148-->
<!--Post: 154--><!--Time: 1086052410-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST154"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 31, 2004 - 6:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Warren b, The page I copied and posted at 9:31 was from ezboard.com and it was titled, Page one of the newest letter recieved 05-05-04.The 8:42am post was from someone who copied the other from a news broadcast on TV as being from the btk. That one I got off of Kansas.com. Both are numbered to 13, when you line them up side by side, they almost tell a story.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 154-->
<!--Post: 192--><!--Time: 1086378650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST192"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 12:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;When you line them up side by side, they almost tell a story&#34;. That&#39;s a very interesting call Sandy &#40;assuming that the second list came from BTK&#41;. <BR>If so,then we have to wonder if there is an underlying message here that BTK was trying to tell.Pure speculation of course but some suggestions :- <BR>1.A serial killer in an all American city. <BR>2.A chilling discovery at Dawn or it begins with a chilling discovery. <BR>3.The killers fetish, to bind torture and strangle <BR>4. Different world colllide, the fantasy and the real! <BR>5.When the search begins&#40;when police know they are dealing with the same killer&#41;, he does a vanishing act. <BR>10.Treasured memories &#40;photographs&#41;in the aftermath. <BR>Perhaps no.11 and 13 are interesting in light of Mike Kelleher&#39;s profile. <BR> <BR> Final curtain call...BTK returns to take one last bow. <BR> <BR>Will there be more,&#40;yes&#41; the author! <BR>Appears to fit with Mike&#39;s assessment.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 192-->
<!--Post: 266--><!--Time: 1086972972-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST266"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jenkins<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jenkins<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 11, 2004 - 9:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The second list &#40;the one that begins all american city&#41; is from Crime Library, it is the titles they gave to the chapters they wrote. BTK had nothing to do with the list that begins All American City.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 266-->
<!--Post: 272--><!--Time: 1087141583-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST272"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 8:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Sean and Jenkins. Did you see the killers note with the upside down &#34;ADDRESS&#34; and the backwards &#34;WRONG&#34; in the shape of a upside down 7 or a L ? Along with DIEEKAF in his puzzle? If the killer wants his puzzle&#39;s to be seen,he should post them here, for sure we like puzzles !<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 272-->
<!--Post: 298--><!--Time: 1087320786-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST298"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 15, 2004 - 10:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I haven&#39;t seen that Sandy, where is it? Thanks<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 298-->
<!--Post: 301--><!--Time: 1087618274-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST301"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 18, 2004 - 9:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Factor X comic books #1 series began in 1995? The BTK letter mentioning factor x was mailed to KAKE in 1978. <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 301-->
<!--Post: 303--><!--Time: 1087641213-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST303"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 19, 2004 - 3:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps BTK meant to communicate that whatever the influence is that comes over him and causes him to commit murder, until we understand what that is, call it factor x.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 303-->
<!--Post: 1080--><!--Time: 1096681811-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1080"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 01, 2004 - 6:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Though having other things to do, I opted to look at Chapter 8 and got the following words &#40;there may be more but my brain stopped&#41;: PJ, JP, follow, cruise, fantasises, telephone co, wpd, worst, team, steam, insurance, realtors, serviceman, std, dog, god, wendie, die, fake id, anna, end, victim, anderson, son, anders, my dna, helm, handyman, end, dam, mad, madd, sex, tops, pot, rye, dash, sad, school, wrong, larry, wichita, poet, doug, tea, spot, sims, builds, nun, ruis, pta, new, poe, office, jo, ed, bore, prowl. <BR> <BR>Taking another approach and looking at multi line/column touching letters only, I got the following: Thelma, Kevin, Aileen, Eileen, Elaine, ignore, typos, french school, museum, model home, sin, tim, simon, novis, fern, lane, cash, pto, oreo, isd, second, syd, bob, fool, sara, idiot, andie, andy, ghost, cash. <BR> <BR>The last group may be meaningless, but it is odd that so many names occur. Perhaps an exercise in futility. <BR> <BR>There are still missing letters, etc, that cannot be discerned. One of those words could be sodomy at the first of the puzzle. Just a guess. It was right above sex. Help is appreciated. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1080-->
<!--Post: 1087--><!--Time: 1096753112-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1087"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, October 02, 2004 - 2:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In a previous post, I questioned that didn&#39;t Factor X comic books #1 series begin in 1995, so there might be no relationship to a 1978 letter by BTK mentioning his own Factor X?  <BR> <BR>However, a friend sent me some information that shows that Factor X was much earlier than I thought. Thanks. <BR>-Deb <BR> <BR>The prototype of X Factor has its very first origins in the 1961 Marvel characters, the Fantastic Four. These four characters got their superhuman characteristics by passing through cosmic rays in their rocket. <BR> <BR>A few years later, due to the popularity of these &#39;superhumans&#39; Marvel comics introduced the Xmen. The X-factor of reference was some indefinable difference in all these characters &#40;whether they be good or bad&#41; that made these characters superhuman mutants &#40;unlike cosmic rays, as in Fantastic Four&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Why &#39;X&#39;? According to the storyline, it was a Charles &#39;X&#39;avier character who scoured around and assembled all these &#39;mutants&#39;. He himself had the superhuman aspect of course - the most powerful telepath. He was referred to as Professor X, and became their leader, etc. <BR> <BR>The disposition of the X characters vascilates between good or bad in some cases, depending the storyline and opponent&#40;s&#41;. <BR> <BR>BTK may have been alluding to a &#39;factor X&#39;.. something that made SKs like himself be able to 1&#41; do what they do, and 2&#41; get away with it. They were invincible.. something which BTK believes also. That is why he has to HELP LE keep movement on the case, otherwise they will give up, and he would lose the &#39;chase&#39;. <BR> <BR>There is also the aspect about Factor X in the comics where they could NOT control themselves.. their abilities took over and they were powerless to stop themselves. BTK&#39;s excuse in one of his letters. <BR> <BR>Fantastic Four: <a href="http://www.brainyencyclopedia.com/encyclopedia/f/fa/fantastic_four.html" target=_top>http://www.brainyencyclopedia.com/encyclopedia/f/f a/fantastic_four.html</a> <BR> <BR>Xmen info: <a href="http://www.brainyencyclopedia.com/encyclopedia/x/x_/x_men.html" target=_top>http://www.brainyencyclopedia.com/encyclopedia/x/x _/x_men.html</a> <BR> <BR>Charles Xavier info: <a href="http://www.brainyencyclopedia.com/encyclopedia/c/ch/charles_xavier.html" target=_top>http://www.brainyencyclopedia.com/encyclopedia/c/c h/charles_xavier.html</a> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
