<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1206"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 14, 2004 - 7:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Still working on Chapter 8. WPD is there. A word following it looks like Dad. If that is true, BTK may have grown up in a law enforcement family and/or military family. With grandfather, father, uncles in a &#39;tradition&#39; of that sort, he could very well have come by his knowledge second hand. Perhaps West Point was a family tradition as well. He would be very adept in all his current skills and still have no &#39;formal&#39; training. He could have inherited books, papers, memorabilia, etc., with someone showing him the ropes. <BR> <BR>If the middle letter is a &#39;u&#39;, it would spell &#39;dud&#39;, perhaps in reference to WPD. The word &#39;gag&#39; appears to be there as well, with its multiple meaning. <BR> <BR>I did find a sentence in the first part of the puzzle: I am worst victim. <BR> <BR>BTK only comes out once in a while. Perhaps we should be looking for the person who goes about his every workaday life: an equally difficult task. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
